  characterName: Amaru Quispe
  promptText: A mining concession targets sacred highland peaks for battery minerals,
    tied to infrastructure pledges like schools. Accepting trades cultural landscapes
    and burial sites for services; refusing preserves heritage but delays promised
    benefits.
  leftAnswer: Infrastructure may deliver urgent services your children need now.
  rightAnswer: Protecting sacred places preserves long-term cultural and ecological
    ties.
